  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Polio and Routine Immunization</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This investment provided core funding of $69 million (2015-21) to the World Health Organization for the Global Polio Eradication Initiative (GPEI). Australia&apos;s contribution provided funding and technical assistance for polio surveillance, monitoring, supplementary immunisation campaigns and outbreak responses. The investment also provided $36 million (2015-18) to a World Bank multi-donor trust fund for countries in Southeast Asia and the Pacific to work towards achieving Universal Health Coverage through strengthened health financing and health service delivery systems. This includes through policy-relevant analytical work, provision of resources for in-country technical assistance, global and regional knowledge sharing, and co-financing of health system strengthening interventions.</narrative>
  </description>
